  "constitutionalAuthorityStatementText": "<pre>\n[Congressional Record Volume 169, Number 116 (Thursday, July 6, 2023)]\n[House]\nFrom the Congressional Record Online through the Government Publishing Office [<a href=\"https://www.gpo.gov\">www.gpo.gov</a>]\nBy Mr. WALBERG:\nH.R. 4468.\nCongress has the power to enact this legislation pursuant\nto the following:\nArticle I, Section 8 of the United States Constitution\nThe single subject of this legislation is:\nTo prohibit the Administrator of the Environmental\nProtection Agency from finalizing, implementing, or enforcing\na proposed rule with respect to emissions from vehicles and\nto preserve consumer choice.\n[Page H3171]\n</pre>",
